{"availability":"available","full":"fixie-ai/ai-jsx","name":"ai-jsx","description":"The AI Application Framework for Javascript","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":1134,"forks":78,"created":"2023-05-30T19:29:07Z","updated":"2024-09-19T23:44:41Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://docs.ai-jsx.com","topics":["ai","jsx","nextjs","react","typescript"],"demo":"https://ai-jsx-nextjs-demo.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:30.851Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:30.851Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:30.851Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:32:30.851Z","stars":1134,"forks":78}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["AI.JSX is a framework for building AI applications using Javascript and JSX. With AI.JSX, you get great tools for prompt engineering and can have the LLM render React components in its response (instead of only text). This means you can provide a set of React components and let the LLM construct your UI dynamically at runtime. AI.JSX also provides native support for tools, Document Question & Answering, and much more.","AI.JSX can be used to create standalone LLM applications that can be deployed anywhere Node.js is supported, or it can be used as part of a larger React application."],"features":["Componetized → LLM prompt engineering through modular, reusable components.","Model Support → Use OpenAI, Anthropic, Llama2, or BYOM. Seamlessly switch between model providers and LLM config (e.g. temperature).","Complete AI Toolbox → Built-in support for Tools, Document Question and Answering, and more.","Generative UI → Seamlessly interweave LLM calls with standard UI components. LLM can dynamically render UI from a set of components you provide.","Streaming → Built-in streaming support."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/fixie-ai/ai-jsx/blob/main/readme.md","fingerprint":"2891134a551459d8ccc95ec6ac1ed0d8b1f6e75ecbd25726